          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The <strong class="text-white">best hydraulic cement</strong> for most basement leaks is <strong class="text-white">DRYLOK Fast Plug</strong>, with Quikrete Hydraulic Water-Stop an equally capable alternative. Use Quikrete FastSet for actively running water, and Xypex Patch'n Plug when the wall is getting a crystalline treatment afterwards.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Whatever is in the tub, the repair depends on technique. Undercut the crack, mix small batches, hold the plug until it sets, then coat the wall and fix the drainage that sent water there in the first place.
          </p>
        </div>

